      "math_academy_id": "e-9208",
      "problem": "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $-0.5$ | $-0.25$ | $0$ | $0.25$ | $0.5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f_X(x)$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ |\n\nLet $Y=2-4X.$ Calculate $P(Y \\gt 2).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's add a $Y = 2-4X$ row to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $-0.5$ | $-0.25$ | $0$ | $0.25$ | $0.5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $4$ | $3$ | $2$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| $f_X(x)$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ |\n\nNow, $f_X(x) = f_Y(y)$ for corresponding values of $X$ and $Y.$ So, the distribution of $Y$ is as follows:\n\n| $y$ | $4$ | $3$ | $2$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f_Y(y)$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y>2) & =P(Y=3)+P(Y=4) \\\\  & =0.2+0.25 \\\\  & =0.45.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
